{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/976877-fictional-pantheon-rules-including-altantis-165-000","id":976877,"title":"Fictional Pantheon rules (including Altantis), $165,000","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-26T19:08:24-07:00","id":976877,"title":"Fictional Pantheon rules (including Altantis), $165,000","content":"As it says on the tin.<br /> <br /> Its the new stretch goal (well okay there a stretch goal at $55,000, but they've nearly reached it already, its for LARPING.<br /> <br /> So fans of Atlantis rejoice its the example Pantheon for Fictional make your own Pantheon rules, so its kind of a two for one deal.<br /> <br /> Personally exploring the possiblities could be fun. I look forward to it, and I think reaching the goal is a safe bet. It could be used to do Monotheistic &quot;pantheons&quot; as well, as someone else here pointed out.<br /> <br /> PS if I ever do a Mage game, I'll likely borrow the Atlantis Pantheon.<br /> <br /> What Fictional Pantheons would you do for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T19:13:17-07:00","id":976878,"title":"","content":"I'd probably mine some from other fantasy settings, honestly. The Elven gods from Dragon Age, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"